---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | ChartGlade"
  description="ChartGlade's privacy policy: we don't collect personal information, analytics stays aggregate, and we run no advertising."
  path="/privacy"
>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  </section>

  <section class="prose">
    <p>The short version: ChartGlade is a static website. We don't collect personal information.</p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing you type, print, or read is sent to us. There are no accounts, no forms beyond an optional email to
      the address on the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>, and no advertising.
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      The site uses two aggregate analytics services: Cloudflare Web Analytics, which measures page views
      without cookies and cannot identify you, and Google Analytics 4, which measures traffic and which
      printables get used. Neither is used for advertising or profiling, and neither is shared with
      advertising networks — there are none.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      Google Analytics sets first-party cookies (<code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_*</code>) to tell
      returning visitors apart in aggregate reports. That is the only cookie use on this site — no
      advertising or cross-site tracking cookies. The site is made for teachers and parents; children
      using printed charts never interact with these cookies.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      Much of this site is for teachers and parents of young children. We knowingly collect no personal
      information from anyone, of any age. If you believe otherwise, please <a href="/contact/">write to us</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Email</h2>
    <p>
      If you email us, we keep your message only to reply, and we never add addresses to lists or share them.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>If this policy changes, the new version appears on this page.</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
